data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `nint` and `nuint` into a `Span`.**

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[4];
```

Both compiled and ran correctly. On this 64-bit system each element is 8 bytes. The only caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context since the size isn't known at compile time — but `stackalloc` itself works fine in safe code when assigned to a `Span`.
